  "degenerate_rule": "An inhabitant of a PROVED law is degenerate iff (a) its state is the model's initial state (its run is empty), or (b) the law is a SORT-site law and the subtrahend of the site's subtraction evaluates to 0 at the inhabitant (its state and action) on the compiled model, so that minuend >= subtrahend holds for every minuend.",
  "doc": "I21 instrument (BUILD_PLAN I21; contract: the docstring of tests_m2/test_audit_extraction.py). Frozen at the prereg: tests_m2/test_audit_extraction.py pins this file's sha256. It fixes what the A2 (hostile input) and A4 (vacuity and over-strength) attacks of audit round M2/2 must cover, and records the committed values the predictions were made from. Computed at the prereg from committed artifacts, nothing run against real code: (1) interface_carriers and codec_labels: every carrier with interface: true and every CODEC edge's partial flag in gen/M2/diagram/*.json; (2) surfaces.sol_loader.call_sites: `grep -n '_loadBatchHeader(' contracts/contracts/l1/rollup/Rollup.sol` in the pinned morph checkout (3e44e795586af3e11285b603ab642c67823add51): 10 calls in 8 external or public functions; the call at :309 (_commitBatchWithBatchData) re-loads batchDataInput.parentBatchHeader, which commitBatch (:259), commitState (:277) and commitBatchWithProof (:402) have already loaded with the same bytes, so no input reaches it that has not passed the same pure loader: it is dominated; (3) reasons and paths: the revert reasons and path counts of load_sol and enc_sol in spec/M2/facts/morph_header.extracted.json (each reason occurs exactly once in contracts/contracts outside test/ and mock/, checked by grep at the pinned commit); (4) surfaces.go_header: the exported methods of (morph-l2/common/batch.BatchHeaderBytes) and (morph-l2/node/types.BatchHeaderBytes) among go.functions of spec/M2/facts/morph_batch.go.extracted.json and morph_nodetypes.go.extracted.json, the sum of their extracted path counts (116 + 107 = 223; validate, unexported, adds 8 per package) and their safe sites (13 + 13); (5) surfaces.batchdata_act: the exported methods of (*morph-l2/common/batch.BatchData) and its open sites in the same document; (6) hypotheses: the keys of results/M2/hypotheses.json; (7) site_law_inhabitants_at_prereg: status, non_vacuity status, run length of the inhabitant's state (non_vacuity.witness.s.run) and its action, from results/M2/L_sort_site_*.json; (8) inputs_sha256: sha256 of each input file at the prereg, on the project branch at 90153fd (after the I19 follow-up A19, which regenerated the rollup and Go documents and gen/M2/coverage.json, and after I59); the Go documents only gained go.globals, so the go_header and batchdata_act values of (4) and (5) are unchanged; (9) surfaces.go_consumer: the Go derivation consumer of the header carrier. UnPackData's four commitBatch branches (node/derivation/derivation.go:617, :639, :662, :664 at 3e44e79) and their selectors, computed as keccak256 of the canonical signature of the ABIs they read (types.BeforeMoveBlockCtxABI and types.LegacyRollupMetaData in node/types/batch.go, node/types/abi/pre_submitter_rollup.json, bindings.RollupMetaData); the open sites of (*Derivation).UnPackData and unpackModernRollupCall in spec/M2/facts/morph_derivation.go.extracted.json; the header steps of (*BatchInfo).ParseBatch from that document's go.calls edges (batch_info.go:92:55 BatchIndex, :96:69 TotalL1MessagePopped); the callers from the same edges (derivation.go:556:28 and :715:32); (10) surfaces.go_consumer.real_inputs, from results/M2/historical/replay.json (I59): each commit's selector is the rollup ABI's 0x41f756da when it has a parent (decoded under the pinned ABI), else that of its legacy_parent.abi_origin commit's IRollup.BatchDataInput (c4794cd: 0xd63b3549, 65b99be: 0x4a8d544f, b755899: 0x428868b5; checked against git show <origin>:contracts/contracts/l1/rollup/IRollup.sol and replay.json abi.history_signatures); parent_281_v0 lists the commits whose parent (or legacy_parent) is a version-0 header of 281 bytes, every one with ok_go false, ok_sol true and pinned_solidity_ok_sol true in replay.json; batch_indices_sha256 is sha256 of their batch indices, ascending, in decimal, joined by ','; (11) representative_search: the bound of A4's search for a non-degenerate inhabitant; reading the model's guards (nothing was run), the shortest non-degenerate runs have length <= 4 (def_bvh_at: one commitBatch; def_w: commitBatch, wait, finalizeBatch; rollup_441: two commitBatch, wait, finalizeBatch; rollup_485_495: commitBatch, wait, finalizeBatch, commitBatch), so 6 leaves slack. The corpora: header_corpus is the empty string plus, for every first byte b0 in 0..255 and every length L in lengths, the byte b0 followed by the first L-1 bytes of sha256(\"I21:<seed>:<b0>:<L>:0\") || sha256(\"I21:<seed>:<b0>:<L>:1\") || ... (ASCII, decimal numbers); 1 + 256 * 10 = 2561 inputs. act_header_corpus is its restriction to first bytes 0, 1, 2, 3 and 255 (51 inputs). encoder_corpus is every version 0..255 with each (prevStateRoot, postStateRoot) in {(0, 0), (0, R2), (R1, 0), (R1, R2)}, R1 = sha256(\"I21:prev\") and R2 = sha256(\"I21:post\") as bytes32: 1024 inputs. A surface's corpus may be larger, never smaller.",
